<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36383" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĭper</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĭpĕris</span></b> , n., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπερι</span> (Sanscr. pippali or
		pippalī, the same), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>pepper.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				7, 14, § 26 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
			27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et piper et quicquid chartis amicitur ineptis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 1, 270</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 2, 417</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14,
				293</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rugosum piper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					5, 55</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrum piper, a term intimating that the miser
					is as sparing of it as if it were something sacred,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6,
					21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of sharp, biting speech: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piper, non homo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 31</span></i>, n. 2.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
